{
  "_doc": "normalize_painting_state (Python) and normalizePaintingState (JS) accept strokes, raster objects and groups the same (docs/scene-state-v2.md 「ペイントのストロークの受け付け方」 and 共通の規則: a text field is a JSON string only, an object field a JSON object only). `strokes`: each case puts base stroke `base` (pen or lasso, below) into layer `layer` with `layerKind` set to it, applies `stroke` (keys set; null removes nothing, it sets null) and `point` (merged into the first point); `expected` null means the stroke is dropped, otherwise the listed keys of the kept stroke are compared (`u0` is the first point's u, compared within 1e-12). `items`: a raster object (`raster`) or group (`group`) with `patch` merged in (`patch` null puts a list in its place); `expected` lists the kept raster objects' [id, layerKind], or the kept groups' [id, actionGroupId].",
